-- title:
--   Every rational place is read at a closed special point (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime subject to the hypothesis `hq3 : q = 3`, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$.
--
--   **Supersingular places and the two function fields.** $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)((t))$ generated by the two $j$-series `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'`) over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the elements of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic curve with invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. The hypothesis `hle` states that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ obtained from the full level-$M'$ modular function field by `laurentBaseChange`, is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'` (the kernel of the unit-group reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`).
--
--   **The constant reduction $R_0$.** $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A$ and with its residue map, the property that every nonzero element can be scaled by a constant into the integers with nonzero residue, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of functions. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Igusa and supersingular valuation rings.** $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `OIg` assigns a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each point of the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, and `OSS` assigns one to each $s \in W$. Their hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which characterises $\mathrm{OIg}(\infty)$ (for `lineInfty q`) as the ring of those $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction and $f \cdot y = x$ after pushing coefficients into $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg`, which produces for each line $\ell$ some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \infty = \ell$ and $\mathrm{OIg}(\ell)$ the pullback of $\mathrm{OIg}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of `OIg`; and `hIg_perm`, which asserts that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $\mathrm{OIg}$ via some permutation of the projective line. On the supersingular side: `hSS_A` says that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over` says that if $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the element $j$ (the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb`) is regular, and if the residue $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$ the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$; `hSS_fix` says each $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ is stable under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t \in \mathrm{OSS}(s)$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   **The regular prolongation.** $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (valuation subring, surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A$, and scaling of nonzero elements into the integers with nonzero residue), with `hR : R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)` and `hR₀O` stating that $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ holds precisely when the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $\mathrm{OIg}(\infty)$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and lies in $A$. A subfield $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\mathbb Q$ carries an element $\pi_0$ with image in $A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hdvr`, `hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and `hκ` requires every $a \in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Moreover $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ has image a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ has image in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ consisting exactly of the elements lying in $A$, assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   **The level field and the model.** `fieldBar q M'` is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Then $F_0$ ranges over the intermediate fields of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying four conditions: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by all constants from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is everything; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every finite family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent and every family $a$ of elements of the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, a relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, i.e. has rational coefficients. Write $T_1$ for the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the image of $K_1$. An $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ is assumed, compatible with the inclusions in the sense that the structure map of $a \in A_1$ has the same image in `fieldBar q M'` as $a$ viewed in $K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$. Next, $j_1 \in T_1$ is an element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the image under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by `coeffEmb` applied to `jq`, and $j_1$ is nonzero. Finally, `NIg` is a finite set of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to that field such that (i) for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $R.\mathrm{residue}$ of it equals $j(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$, and (ii) a place $Q$ belongs to `NIg` exactly when there is $s \in W$ with $g \in s.\mathrm{toValuationSubring} \iff j(g) \in Q.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$ for all $g$.
--
--   The scheme in play is [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along their common middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ and chart morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf`.
--
--   **Local abbreviations.** For a point $x$ of the model and $f \in T_1$, `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of either chart with $\iota$-image $x$ there are $g,h$ in the corresponding chart algebra with $h \notin y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ and $f h = g$ in $T_1$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational and that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in $P.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ iff `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x` collects five clauses: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ is closed, in that $x \rightsquigarrow y$ implies $y = x$; for each chart point $y$ over $x$, every chart element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a nonunit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ (one clause for each of the two charts); and, for each point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, each algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and each ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ avoids `ssJSet q Ω`. `Reads x Q` says that for every $f \in T_1$ with `InStalk x f`, the image of $f$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its residue $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in $Q.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$, and that residue is a nonunit of $Q.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$ precisely when `InMax x f`. `OffBranch x` says that for every line $\ell \ne \infty$ and every chart point $y$ over $x$ (in either chart) there is a chart element whose image is a nonunit of $\mathrm{OIg}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ that is rational (the structure map to its residue field is surjective), there exists a point $x$ of `TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁` such that: (1) `toBase` maps $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; (2) $x \rightsquigarrow y$ implies $y = x$, so $x$ is a closed point; (3) for every point $y$ of the finite chart with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$-image $x$, every element of `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a nonunit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; (4) the same holds for the chart at infinity with `chartAlgInf` and $\iota_{\mathrm{Inf}}$; and (5) `Reads x Q` holds.
--
--   Thus the first four conjuncts of the conclusion are the first four clauses of `GoodPt`, the supersingularity clause of `GoodPt` being absent, while `Centred` and `OffBranch`, although introduced, are not asserted.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ case of the existence of closed special points of the two-chart integral model that read off a prescribed rational place of the reduced Igusa field: on the $\infty$-branch of the Igusa covering the reduction is an isomorphism at $q = 3$, so the reduced field is the level-$M'$ field and every rational place is realised. It is the input to [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three), where the supersingularity and off-branch conditions are added, and it relies on the properness of `toBase` for this model, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isProper_toBase_twoChartIntegralModel_levelField_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isProper_toBase_twoChartIntegralModel_levelField_of_eq_three).
